// Title: Potential Privilege Escalation Using Symlink Between Osk and Cmd
// Sigma ID: e9b61244-893f-427c-b287-3e708f321c6b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-12-11 | Modified: 2022-12-20
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1546.008
// Description: Detects the creation of a symbolic link between "cmd.exe" and the accessibility on-screen
//   keyboard binary (osk.exe) using "mklink". This technique provides an elevated command prompt to
//   the user from the login screen without the need to log in.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/5c1e6f1b4fafd01c8d1ece85f510160fc1275fbf/atomics/T1546.008/T1546.008.md
//   - https://ss64.com/nt/mklink.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_cmd_mklink_osk_cmd.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "Cmd.Exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "mklink" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\osk.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\cmd.exe")
